{"availability":"available","full":"ronakrupani/nura-marketing-site","name":"nura-marketing-site","description":"Marketing site for Nura, a voice companion for older adults living with dementia and memory loss. The landing page is a working demo: it answers only from what a family wrote down, and says so plainly when nothing matches.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-10T19:10:49Z","updated":"2026-10-04T22:56:27Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://nura-six-alpha.vercel.app","topics":["accessibility","anthropic","claude","dementia","framer-motion","marketing-site","nextjs","react","supabase","tailwindcss","typescript"],"demo":"https://nura-six-alpha.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:49.381Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:49.381Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:49.381Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:01:49.381Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Marketing site for Nura, a voice companion for older adults living with dementia, Alzheimer's, and memory loss. A family writes down facts about their relative's life; the relative asks questions out loud and hears those answers back, warmly, every time they ask.","The whole point of the product is that it never makes anything up, so the site is built around a demo that lets you watch that happen rather than read a claim about it. You can see the memories a fictional family wrote, type your own question, and get back a real answer with the source memory printed underneath it. One of the suggested questions has no matching memory on purpose, so you can watch Nura decline to guess.","This repository is the marketing site only. There is no login and no product here. Two routes do real work: /api/ask runs the demo, and /api/waitlist inserts an email into a Supabase waitlist table server-side."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ronakrupani/nura-marketing-site/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c9f0e632eac859e2bfa1c1c5c69545c4a22736b5b5d5e93e164ca44980250d2c","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:49.457Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:49.457Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Marketing site for Nura, a voice companion for older adults living with dementia, Alzheimer's, and memory loss. A family writes down facts about their relative's life; the relative asks questions out loud and hears those answers back, warmly, every time they ask.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ronakrupani/nura-marketing-site/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"There is no login and no product here.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ronakrupani/nura-marketing-site/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"c9f0e632eac859e2bfa1c1c5c69545c4a22736b5b5d5e93e164ca44980250d2c","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ronakrupani/nura-marketing-site/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:49.457Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T22:56:27Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ronakrupani/nura-marketing-site/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:49.458Z","hash":"c9f0e632eac859e2bfa1c1c5c69545c4a22736b5b5d5e93e164ca44980250d2c","originalBytes":7369,"storedBytes":7369,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["memory","one","question","demo","nura","answer","api","it.","only","run","after","colour","memories","model","npm","site","there","warm","answered","fallback","family","never","system","waitlist","bash","content","every","exactly","guarantee","key","lib","live","marketing","phrase","questions","rather","real","runs","should","supabase","they","three","without","wrote","about","adding","ambiguous","answer.ts","any","anything","ask","back","both","changing","check","const","deterministic","does","each","email","engine","ever","everything","fails","figtree","files","happen","lives","makes","map","match",